# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# A stutter on demand (the Sections screen's K3): right queues a complex one, left a simple one, the middle none; it
# plays on the next group's last bar that isn't an intro's or an outro's, then K3 shows OFF again. The first song is
# 56 bars at 81 BPM (2963 ms a bar): an 8-bar intro, four 8-bar grooves (no lead), two lead blocks. Queued in the
# intro's second bar, it waits out the intro and lands on the first groove's last bar (bar 16, from 0: 15), a bar the
# song's own stutters skip (its first pass without the lead).
listen
wait 1400
tap PLAY
wait 3000
tap SEL
wait 50
said SECTIONS
expect stutter 0
spin K3 1
wait 50
said STUTTER COMPLEX
expect stutter 2
# back to the middle: cancelled
spin K3 -1
wait 50
said STUTTER OFF
expect stutter 0
# left: a simple one; right past the middle: a complex one instead
spin K3 -1
wait 50
said STUTTER SIMPLE
expect stutter 1
spin K3 2
wait 50
said STUTTER COMPLEX
expect stutter 2
shot stutter-queued.png
# the intro passes; it waits (bar 12, from 0: 11, about 34.6 s in)
wait 30000
expect section 1
expect stutter 2
expect stutter_bar -1
# the first groove's last bar (bar 16, from 0: 15; 45.9-48.9 s): it lands there, a complex figure
wait 12800
expect bar 15
expect stutter_bar 15
expect stutter_fig >2
expect stutter 2
# its replays (the bar's 15th 16th, about 48.6 s): the mix stutters
wait 1050
expect stuttering 1
# the next bar: played, OFF again, nothing waiting
wait 2000
expect bar 16
expect stutter 0
expect stutter_bar -1
shot stutter-played.png
